==== HOW TO READ IT ====
  Fold ONLY this log:  python3 notes/parse_sweep_logs.py haoyang_logs/coarse_tilesize_20260804_013002.log
  (never re-parse haoyang_logs/* -- 10 curated logs are gone from disk and 189
   records survive only inside sweep_records.json)

  Build the residual grid, then read it two ways:
    ACROSS a row (fixed M, t varies)   -> tile count varies, rows/core varies
    DOWN  a column (fixed t, M varies) -> rows/core varies, tile count FIXED
  The column direction is the new information: it is the only place rows/core
  moves with t held still. Subtract each M's t=1 anchor first.

  If the residual tracks rows/core, the fix belongs in the coarse residency
  term (_lx_spill_bw_derate, currently gated OFF for matmul) rather than in a
  new per-iteration term.
